  "steps": [
    {
      "say": "Here is a simple wooden chair. It looks plain, but every piece has a job. Together they hold you up safely every time you sit down. Let's take it apart and see how!",
      "do": [
        {
          "reveal": [
            "seat",
            "leg_fl",
            "leg_fr",
            "leg_bl",
            "leg_br",
            "apron_front",
            "apron_back",
            "apron_left",
            "apron_right",
            "stretcher_left",
            "stretcher_right",
            "rail_lower",
            "rail_top",
            "slat_left",
            "slat_mid",
            "slat_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "First, the four legs. When you sit, your weight pushes down, and the legs carry it straight to the floor, like four friends each holding one corner of a heavy box. Four corners spread out make it hard to tip over.",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": "all"
        },
        {
          "label": [
            "leg_fl",
            "leg_fr",
            "leg_bl",
            "leg_br"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "leg_fl",
            "leg_fr",
            "leg_bl",
            "leg_br"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "leg_fl"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Legs alone would wobble and splay apart. So rails called aprons join the tops of the legs in a square frame, and stretchers tie them together lower down. It's like holding hands in a circle so nobody falls over.",
      "do": [
        {
          "label": [
            "apron_front",
            "apron_back",
            "apron_left",
            "apron_right",
            "stretcher_left",
            "stretcher_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "apron_front",
            "apron_back",
            "apron_left",
            "apron_right",
            "stretcher_left",
            "stretcher_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "apron_left"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "The seat rests on top of the apron frame and the legs. It spreads your weight out over the whole frame, the way a tray spreads the load of a pile of books.",
      "do": [
        {
          "label": [
            "seat"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "seat"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "seat"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Look how the back legs keep going up past the seat. Two rails run between them, and slats fill the gap. When you lean back, the slats push on the rails, and the rails pass that push into the tall back legs.",
      "do": [
        {
          "label": [
            "rail_top",
            "rail_lower",
            "slat_left",
            "slat_mid",
            "slat_right"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "rail_top",
            "rail_lower",
            "slat_left",
            "slat_mid",
            "slat_right",
            "leg_bl",
            "leg_br"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "rail_top"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Now let's put it all back together. Legs, frame, seat and back all lock into each other, so the chair works as one strong, steady team.",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": []
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "recap": "A chair stays strong because its legs carry your weight to the floor while rails tie the legs into a steady frame.",
  "question": "Have you ever wondered why some stools only need three legs to stand without wobbling?",
  "layout": {
    "template": "blueprint",
    "explode": "free"
  }
